# Append-only coordination surfaces.
#
# plan.md (§ Decisions / Discovered) and SKILLS.md are written by many agents
# concurrently, each appending its own rows. A default three-way merge treats two
# independent appends at the file tail as a conflict, so every concurrent PR pair
# collides on a file where both sides are always wanted.
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides instead of conflicting. That is the semantically
# correct resolution for an append-only log and matches the AGENTS.md rule that
# these logs are never rewritten, only extended.
#
# Measured on 2026-08-06: 8 of 11 CONFLICTING open PRs were blocked solely by
# these two files (plan.md x5, SKILLS.md x3) — zero real code conflicts among them.
plan.md    merge=union
SKILLS.md  merge=union
